-- Refresh two table comments after the write-door fixes, so the database keeps describing itself truthfully. Comments
-- only: the table comments of external_listings and vehicle_quality_scores are replaced with the live text that
-- 20261008000000_describe_external_listings.sql and 20261008001000_describe_vehicle_quality_scores.sql set, except the
-- sentences about the two writers fixed since; for the same reason the column comments external_listings.final_price
-- and external_listings.updated_at lose their present-tense mention of the retired function. Every other character is
-- kept (25 of 25 and 20 of 20 columns stay described).
-- Describe stage of the repair loop (docs/ledger/theory/data-machine-cases.md section 12; data-machine.md "the database
-- describes itself").
--
-- REASONS:
--   1. enrich_cross_ref_ext_price(integer) is RETIRED since 2026-10-07:
--   20261008005000_retire_enrich_cross_ref_ext_price.sql (PR #806) revoked EXECUTE from PUBLIC, anon, authenticated and
--   service_role and kept the body. The external_listings comment still counted it among seven SECURITY DEFINER
--   functions open to anon and said anyone with the public API key could trigger its write to vehicles.sale_price; the
--   final_price and updated_at column comments still named it as a live reader.
--   2. The deployment of the edge function backfill-quality-scores is no longer the unguarded version 26: commit
--   0e4fad07a (PR #808) deployed a guarded stub as version 27 at 2026-10-07 13:26:48Z. The vehicle_quality_scores
--   comment still said version 26 was ACTIVE with no write guard and that any bodiless request scores 500 vehicles.
--
-- METHOD (read 2026-10-07 13:44-13:50Z UTC):
--   The live comments from pg_description (obj_description, col_description), compared with the texts of 20261008000000
--   and 20261008001000 at origin/main e791d7f1a: identical (5,648, 3,848, 1,039 and 984 characters). The ACLs of the
--   seven SECURITY DEFINER functions that read external_listings, from pg_proc.proacl and has_function_privilege at
--   13:44Z: enrich_cross_ref_ext_price {postgres=X/postgres} (anon, authenticated and service_role false);
--   get_vehicle_profile_data, vehicle_price_signal, get_listings_needing_sync, calculate_platform_revenue,
--   check_auction_sync_health and check_sync_coverage still grant EXECUTE to PUBLIC, anon, authenticated and
--   service_role. The deployment of backfill-quality-scores from the management API (version 27, ACTIVE, verify_jwt
--   false, updated 2026-10-07 13:26:48Z) and its source at origin/main
--   (supabase/functions/backfill-quality-scores/index.ts: OPTIONS gets 204, every other request passes requireWriteAuth
--   and then gets 410 Gone; no write path). A logged-out GET at 13:44Z answered HTTP 401 ("Anonymous calls are not
--   accepted here"); vehicle_quality_scores held 625,154 rows with the newest created 2026-10-07 05:42:11Z before and
--   after it. The new comments are built by replacing those sentences in the live text.
-- LIMITS:
--   The rest of both comments keeps its 2026-10-07 counts and read times as they were; nothing else was re-measured.
--   Whether the backfill-quality-scores deployment is deleted is the owner's call (the orphan-deletion batch).
-- CHANGED EXISTING COMMENTS:
--   external_listings table: "Seven SECURITY DEFINER functions open to anon ... and
--   enrich_cross_ref_ext_price(integer), which has no fixed search_path, UPDATEs vehicles.sale_price from final_price
--   for vehicles whose sale_price is NULL (116 of 6,791 rows of a 5% block sample qualify, 1.7%), so anyone with the
--   public API key can trigger that write." now reads six such functions, and a sentence says the seventh is RETIRED
--   and by which migration.
--   external_listings.final_price: "enrich_cross_ref_ext_price copies it to vehicles.sale_price where that is NULL,
--   without currency." is now in the past tense with the retirement. external_listings.updated_at: "Read as the recency
--   key by vehicle_price_signal and enrich_cross_ref_ext_price." now says the latter only until its retirement.
--   vehicle_quality_scores table: "... its version 26 (deployed 2026-03-20) is still ACTIVE with verify_jwt false and
--   no write guard, and any request without a body scores the 500 newest vehicles that lack a row ..." now says version
--   26 stayed ACTIVE until 2026-10-07 and that the deployment is the guarded 410 stub since 13:26Z, so no writer fires
--   on a GET, with the probe; "It writes only" became "The retired function wrote only".

BEGIN;
SET LOCAL statement_timeout = '30s';
SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '5s';

COMMENT ON TABLE public.external_listings IS
'RETIRED in favor of vehicle_events (commit 216f9c545, 2026-03-07, moved its writers there; no row created since 2026-04-14). Legacy listing table: one row per listing of a vehicle on an auction or sale platform (grain: one platform listing; listing_url and listing_url_key are distinct on every row). 139,760 rows on 2026-10-07 for 137,844 vehicle ids. By platform: bat 103,978, barrettjackson 25,752, pcarmarket 6,224, bonhams 2,066, cars_and_bids 1,275, mecum 273, collecting_cars 70, sbx 38, broad_arrow 31, rmsothebys 22, classic_com 11, gooding 9, hagerty 7, blocket 3, craigslist 1. By listing_status: sold 109,831, ended 25,716, active 4,038 (stale), unsold 142, pending 28, cancelled 5. Created 2025-12-07 .. 2026-04-14 (by month: 2025-12 1,620, 2026-01 34,989, 2026-02 96,289, 2026-03 6,625, 2026-04 237) by the extractors (extract-bat-core, extract-barrett-jackson, extract-bonhams, import-pcarmarket-listing, extract-cars-and-bids-core, extract-mecum, extract-broad-arrow, extract-gooding and others); after commit 216f9c545 the deployed copies still inserted bat rows until 2026-03-07 23:04Z, bonhams until 2026-03-15 and pcarmarket until 2026-04-14. In a 5% block sample 6,724 of 6,791 rows (99.0%) have a vehicle_events row with the same source_url. Writers today (pipeline_registry owner retired, do_not_write_directly true): the trigger sync_bid_count_trigger on vehicles (AFTER UPDATE OF bid_count) runs sync_bid_count_to_external_listings, which raises bid_count and stamps updated_at on the listings of the vehicle whose count is lower; it made the 3 updates after 2026-04-14 (2026-09-27 twice and 2026-10-06 00:49Z; each row now carries the vehicle bid_count). merge_vehicle_into_primary_by_url moves vehicle_id to the surviving vehicle or deletes the row when the survivor already holds the same platform and listing_id, without touching updated_at. Maintenance functions that write it have no caller in cron.job or the repo: reconcile_listing_status (its cron job reconcile-listing-status, jobid 184, is inactive), cleanup_stale_listings, fix_external_listings_missing_prices, merge_duplicate_listings and backfill_missing_bat_external_listings. pg_stat_user_tables since its counters began (the server last started 2026-09-29 09:20Z): 0 inserts, 2 updates and 0 deletes; 18 sequential scans; index scans 1,197,694 at 12:49Z and 1,200,743 at 12:58Z, reads that keep arriving (the bid-count trigger probes the table by vehicle_id on every vehicles bid_count change). Five triggers fire on writes here: trg_external_listings_url_key (BEFORE; sets listing_url_key), track_auction_transitions (timeline events through create_auction_timeline_event when the status changes), trg_sync_external_listing_to_org_vehicles (organization_vehicles links), trigger_auto_mark_vehicle_sold (vehicles sale fields and an organization_vehicles sold_by row when sold) and trigger_sync_active_auction_prices (vehicles high_bid and bid_count while active). Readers: get_vehicle_profile_data(uuid) (called by the vehicle profile page, nuke_frontend/src/pages/vehicle-profile/loadVehicleData.ts, which ignores this part of the result), vehicle_price_signal(uuid[]) (DiscoveryFeed, PriceAnalysisPanel; active rows), compute_vehicle_grade (extract-bat-core, persist_vehicle_grade), score_closed_predictions (score-live-auctions), get_vehicle_current_price (on_user_follows_vehicle), apply_approved_verification (trigger on vehicle_relationship_verifications), the view sold_vehicle_proof (SoldInventoryBrowser.tsx), and about 20 other function bodies with no caller in cron.job or the repo. The frontend now reads vehicle_events into an external_listings-shaped object and does not query this table (OrganizationProfile.tsx records the switch). Foreign keys in: auction_listing_images.external_listing_id (ON DELETE SET NULL, 367 rows) and external_auction_bids.external_listing_id (ON DELETE CASCADE, 1 of 26,164 rows). Defects (2026-10-07): 14,422 rows (10.3%) point at a vehicle id that is not in vehicles (see vehicle_id); platform matches observation_sources.slug on 81.5% of rows (see platform); 1,920 pcarmarket, 10 bat and 8 cars_and_bids sold rows carry the write clock as sold_at (see sold_at); 1,671 rows name the auction house as organization_id, and the triggers recorded it as the seller (see organization_id). Access: RLS is on with no policy, and anon and authenticated hold no privilege on the table or any column (2026-10-07). Six SECURITY DEFINER functions open to anon (EXECUTE granted to PUBLIC, anon and authenticated) go around that: get_vehicle_profile_data returns every column of every row of any public vehicle, metadata with the seller and buyer handles included; vehicle_price_signal returns listing_url and current_bid of active rows; get_listings_needing_sync returns id, platform and listing_url of active rows; calculate_platform_revenue, check_auction_sync_health and check_sync_coverage return aggregates. A seventh, enrich_cross_ref_ext_price(integer), which UPDATEd vehicles.sale_price from final_price wherever sale_price was NULL and which anyone with the public API key could run, is RETIRED since 2026-10-07: 20261008005000 revoked EXECUTE from PUBLIC, anon, authenticated and service_role, so no API role can call it (its body is kept). The view sold_vehicle_proof (owner postgres, not security_invoker, SELECT granted to anon and authenticated) shows listing_url, platform, status, final_price, sold_at and end_date of 460 rows. No write receipts. Clocks: start_date, end_date and sold_at are event times on the platform as the extractor parsed them; created_at, updated_at and last_synced_at are database or writer times; nothing records when a value was read from the site.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.final_price IS
'Hammer or sale price, numeric, nullable. Filled on 110,461 rows (79.0%, 2026-10-07): 109,590 sold rows and 871 others (pcarmarket 669, bat 176, 26 on other platforms); NULL on 241 sold rows. By platform: bat 80,785 (median 22,500), barrettjackson 25,431 (median 44,000), pcarmarket 2,585, bonhams 1,042, cars_and_bids 610, mecum 5, blocket 3. All whole numbers but one, none 0 or below. The currency is not stored: the US platforms sell in US dollars, the 3 blocket values are Swedish kronor by magnitude, and the 1,042 bonhams prices carry no currency (the bonhams rows that record one in metadata.estimate_currency say GBP 260, EUR 126, CHF 22, USD 1, none of them priced). auto_mark_vehicle_sold_from_external_listing copies it (or current_bid) to vehicles.sale_price, winning_bid and high_bid when sold; enrich_cross_ref_ext_price copied it to vehicles.sale_price where that was NULL, without currency, until 20261008005000 retired that function (EXECUTE revoked from every API role, 2026-10-07). Unit: the platform sale currency, not stored on the row. Source: the extractor. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: as of updated_at.';

COMMENT ON COLUMN public.external_listings.updated_at IS
'When a writer last stamped the row, timestamptz, nullable, default now(). No update trigger maintains it: the extractors sent their own clock (extract-bat-core sent new Date() with every insert and update) and sync_bid_count_to_external_listings sets now(); merge_vehicle_into_primary_by_url leaves it unchanged. Filled on every row (2026-10-07). By month: 2025-12 138, 2026-01 10,130, 2026-02 112,881, 2026-03 15,702, 2026-04 906, 2026-09 2, 2026-10 1; the 3 rows after 2026-04 were stamped by the bid-count trigger. Equal to created_at on 27,899 rows, later on 84,455 and earlier on 27,406 (19.6%: bat 25,126, pcarmarket 2,006; by a median of 0.07 s on bat and 0.10 s on pcarmarket, at most 63 s), consistent with the extractor stamping its own clock before the insert reached the database. Read as the recency key by vehicle_price_signal, and by enrich_cross_ref_ext_price until 20261008005000 retired it (2026-10-07). Unit: timestamptz. Source: the writer clock. Grain: one platform listing. Clock: writer time of the last write.';

COMMENT ON TABLE public.vehicle_quality_scores IS
'Automated quality tracking - identifies incomplete listings and triggers repairs: one completeness snapshot per vehicle (grain: one vehicle; PRIMARY KEY vehicle_id), upserted in place, so it keeps the latest write only. 625,154 rows on 2026-10-07 (the atlas estimate of 624,342 is a stale reltuples). Nothing recomputes it: 622,554 rows (99.6%) come from two bulk statements on 2026-02-06 (369,759 rows at 16:26:24Z and 252,795 at 17:12:03Z) whose SQL is in no repo file and no logged migration, and they have not changed since. The two passes used different rules: the first set has_vin, has_price, has_images, image_count and has_mileage and left every needs_* flag false; the second set has_price, needs_vin_lookup on every row and needs_price_backfill, and left has_vin, has_images and has_mileage false. The other 2,600 rows were written one at a time by the edge function backfill-quality-scores: 1,061 on 2026-02-06 (all with score 0), 30 on 2026-02-07 and 9 on 2026-02-14 (Saturday 03:00Z runs of the cron job analytics-quality-scores, jobid 135, now inactive), and 500 each on 2026-03-20, 2026-09-30 and 2026-10-07. Its source left the repo in commit 200581de7 (2026-03-31), but its version 26 (deployed 2026-03-20, verify_jwt false, no write guard) stayed ACTIVE until 2026-10-07 and scored the 500 newest vehicles that lacked a row on any request without a body: the 2026-10-07 05:40Z batch came from an unauthenticated GET in a curl sweep that called every deployed function in turn, and the 2026-09-30 20:25Z batch ran during a similar GET sweep by a node client (edge and function logs, read 2026-10-07). Since 2026-10-07 13:26Z the deployment is the guarded stub of commit 0e4fad07a (version 27): every request except OPTIONS must pass requireWriteAuth and then gets 410 Gone, so no writer fires on a GET (a logged-out GET answered 401 at 13:44Z, and the table stayed at 625,154 rows, newest 05:42Z). The retired function wrote only vehicle_id, overall_score, last_checked_at and updated_at, so its rows keep the defaults in every other column. Never written on any row (2026-10-07): has_events, event_count, bat_image_count, dropbox_image_count, issues (an empty array), needs_bat_images, needs_deletion and last_repaired_at. Coverage (1% block sample of vehicles): 2,653 of 6,754 vehicles that are not soft-deleted (39.3%) have a row, and 10 of the 4,111 created after the 2026-02-06 passes. Orphans: 578 of 5,137 rows of a 1% block sample (11.3%, about 70,000 rows) point at a vehicle id that is not in vehicles, although the foreign key to vehicles (ON DELETE CASCADE) is validated and its triggers are enabled, so those vehicles were deleted with the RI triggers off; the exact count exceeded the 10 s timeout. Of the sampled rows whose vehicle exists, 2,244 of 4,559 (49.2%) belong to a soft-deleted vehicle (1,292 of the 1,631 rows of the second pass). pg_stat_user_tables since its counters began (the server last started 2026-09-29 09:20Z; read 13:05Z): 1,000 inserts (the two 500-row batches), 0 updates, 0 deletes, 10 sequential and 2,092 index scans. Readers: none live. auto_queue_backfills (trigger trg_auto_queue_backfills on scraper_versions, which had 0 writes since the counters began), calculate_verification_layer (reached only through refresh_platform_tier, which no trigger, cron job or code calls) and queue_vehicle_for_backfill (no caller) read overall_score; the views repair_queue and vehicles_needing_micro_scrape read it, and nothing reads them; scripts/backfill-single-vehicle.js and scripts/check-progress.sh read it by hand. pipeline_registry (owned_by unknown, do_not_write_directly true) lists it as a drop-list candidate; recorded here as a fact, not decided. Access: RLS is on with no policy and anon and authenticated hold no privilege (revoked by the logged migration 20260314031411 rls_lockdown_internal_tables, which is not in the repo); the two views are closed to both roles as well. No write receipts. Clocks: created_at is the database clock of the insert; updated_at and last_checked_at are the writer clock (equal to created_at on the bulk rows); nothing records which state of the vehicle a row was computed from.';

DO $$
DECLARE
  missing text;
BEGIN
  SELECT string_agg(c.relname || '.' || a.attname, ', ' ORDER BY c.relname, a.attnum) INTO missing
  FROM pg_attribute a
  JOIN pg_class c ON c.oid = a.attrelid
  WHERE a.attrelid IN ('public.external_listings'::regclass, 'public.vehicle_quality_scores'::regclass)
    AND a.attnum > 0
    AND NOT a.attisdropped
    AND col_description(a.attrelid, a.attnum) IS NULL;
  IF missing IS NULL THEN
    RAISE NOTICE 'external_listings and vehicle_quality_scores: every column has a comment';
  ELSE
    RAISE NOTICE 'columns still without a comment: %', missing;
  END IF;
END
$$;

COMMIT;
